{"name":"Screaming Skull","hex":"#f0f2d2","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"screaming","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Loud, sharp, and piercing to the ear.","Obvious; distinct."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A scream."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/screaming"},{"term":"skull","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The main bones of the head considered as a unit; including the cranium, facial bones, and mandible.","These bones as a symbol for death; death's-head."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit in the head with a fist, a weapon, or a thrown object.","To strike the top of (the ball)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skull"}],"entries":[{"title":"Screaming skull","blocks":[{"text":"A screaming skull is a paranormal object, a human skull which per legend speaks, screams, or otherwise haunts its environs. The legend is mostly found in England and other English-speaking regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Attacking_skull_in_The_Screaming_Skull_%2801.02.48%29.jpg/330px-Attacking_skull_in_The_Screaming_Skull_%2801.02.48%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Screaming_skull"},{"title":"Screaming","blocks":[{"text":"A scream is a loud/hard vocalization in which air is passed through the vocal cords with greater force than in regular or close-distance vocalisation. This can be performed by any creature possessing lungs, including humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Baby_yelling.jpg/330px-Baby_yelling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Screaming"},{"title":"Skull","blocks":[{"text":"The skull, or cranium, is typically a bony enclosure around the brain of a vertebrate. In some fish and amphibians, the skull is of cartilage. The skull is at the head end